== 6d02a43a75cd3364b3c230e9070f1413e60f0d02
19:Make sure that you use the same base model in the `FROM` command as you used to create the adapter otherwise you will get erratic results. Most frameworks use different quantization methods, so it'
111:## Quantizing a Model
113:Quantizing a model allows you to run models faster and with less memory consumption but at reduced accuracy. This allows you to run a model on more modest hardware.
115:Ollama can quantize FP16 and FP32 based models into different quantization levels using the `-q/--quantize` flag with the `ollama create` command.
117:First, create a Modelfile with the FP16 or FP32 based model you wish to quantize.
123:Use `ollama create` to then create the quantized model.
126:$ ollama create --quantize q4_K_M mymodel
128:quantizing F16 model to Q4_K_M
135:### Supported Quantizations
139:#### K-means Quantizations
